  "captions": [
    {
      "id": "cap-hook-1",
      "kind": "caption",
      "beatId": "hook-1",
      "label": "Cold air is not made. It is moved. Every",
      "text": "Cold air is not made. It is moved. Every air conditioner and every heat pump does one thing — it picks heat up in one place and puts it down in another.",
      "startMs": 700,
      "durationMs": 8902
    },
    {
      "id": "cap-hook-2",
      "kind": "caption",
      "beatId": "hook-2",
      "label": "One substance does the carrying. It trav",
      "text": "One substance does the carrying. It travels a closed loop, over and over, and changes state four times on the way around.",
      "startMs": 10802,
      "durationMs": 7104
    },
    {
      "id": "cap-hook-3",
      "kind": "caption",
      "beatId": "hook-3",
      "label": "Learn those four legs and every diagnosi",
      "text": "Learn those four legs and every diagnosis you will ever make has somewhere to start.",
      "startMs": 18606,
      "durationMs": 4034
    },
    {
      "id": "cap-s0-1",
      "kind": "caption",
      "beatId": "s0-1",
      "label": "Three states, three colours, and they me",
      "text": "Three states, three colours, and they mean the same thing in every episode. Hot vapor. High-pressure liquid. Cool vapor. Watch where each one lives.",
      "startMs": 23840,
      "durationMs": 9631
    },
    {
      "id": "cap-s1-1",
      "kind": "caption",
      "beatId": "s1-1",
      "label": "Start at the compressor. Cool, low-press",
      "text": "Start at the compressor. Cool, low-pressure vapor arrives from the suction line.",
      "startMs": 34171,
      "durationMs": 4520
    },
    {
      "id": "cap-s1-2",
      "kind": "caption",
      "beatId": "s1-2",
      "label": "The compressor squeezes it. Pressure goe",
      "text": "The compressor squeezes it. Pressure goes up, and temperature goes up with it — not because the compressor made heat, but because the same heat is now packed into far less space.",
      "startMs": 39391,
      "durationMs": 9244
    },
    {
      "id": "cap-s1-3",
      "kind": "caption",
      "beatId": "s1-3",
      "label": "What leaves is hot, high-pressure vapor,",
      "text": "What leaves is hot, high-pressure vapor, and it is now hotter than the outdoor air. That is the whole trick. Heat only moves from hot to cold, so we made the refrigerant the hot one.",
      "startMs": 49835,
      "durationMs": 9562
    },
    {
      "id": "cap-s2-1",
      "kind": "caption",
      "beatId": "s2-1",
      "label": "That hot vapor runs to the condenser coi",
      "text": "That hot vapor runs to the condenser coil, and outdoor air blows across the fins.",
      "startMs": 60597,
      "durationMs": 4679
    },
    {
      "id": "cap-s2-2",
      "kind": "caption",
      "beatId": "s2-2",
      "label": "The refrigerant gives its heat up to tha",
      "text": "The refrigerant gives its heat up to that air, and as it does, it condenses — vapor to liquid, at nearly constant pressure.",
      "startMs": 65976,
      "durationMs": 7403
    },
    {
      "id": "cap-s2-3",
      "kind": "caption",
      "beatId": "s2-3",
      "label": "It leaves as high-pressure liquid. Still",
      "text": "It leaves as high-pressure liquid. Still warm, but a liquid now. The colour change on the diagram is a change of state, not a change of temperature.",
      "startMs": 74079,
      "durationMs": 8642
    },
    {
      "id": "cap-s3-1",
      "kind": "caption",
      "beatId": "s3-1",
      "label": "Next comes the metering device — a therm",
      "text": "Next comes the metering device — a thermostatic expansion valve, or a fixed orifice. Either way, it is a deliberate restriction.",
      "startMs": 83421,
      "durationMs": 7590
    },
    {
      "id": "cap-s3-2",
      "kind": "caption",
      "beatId": "s3-2",
      "label": "Liquid is forced through a small opening",
      "text": "Liquid is forced through a small opening into a much lower pressure. Some of it flashes to vapor immediately, and flashing pulls heat out of what is left behind.",
      "startMs": 91711,
      "durationMs": 8678
    },
    {
      "id": "cap-s3-3",
      "kind": "caption",
      "beatId": "s3-3",
      "label": "So what comes out the far side is cold. ",
      "text": "So what comes out the far side is cold. That is where the cold in air conditioning is actually created. Not at the compressor — here.",
      "startMs": 101589,
      "durationMs": 7427
    },
    {
      "id": "cap-s4-1",
      "kind": "caption",
      "beatId": "s4-1",
      "label": "That cold mixture enters the evaporator ",
      "text": "That cold mixture enters the evaporator coil, inside the house, with return air blowing across it.",
      "startMs": 110216,
      "durationMs": 5366
    },
    {
      "id": "cap-s4-2",
      "kind": "caption",
      "beatId": "s4-2",
      "label": "Now the refrigerant is colder than the a",
      "text": "Now the refrigerant is colder than the air, so heat moves the other way — out of your air, into the refrigerant, boiling it from liquid back to vapor.",
      "startMs": 116282,
      "durationMs": 8597
    },
    {
      "id": "cap-s4-3",
      "kind": "caption",
      "beatId": "s4-3",
      "label": "The air leaves that coil about twenty de",
      "text": "The air leaves that coil about twenty degrees cooler than it arrived, and drier, because water condensed on the cold fins and ran out the drain.",
      "startMs": 126079,
      "durationMs": 7611
    },
    {
      "id": "cap-s5-1",
      "kind": "caption",
      "beatId": "s5-1",
      "label": "The vapor leaves the evaporator cool and",
      "text": "The vapor leaves the evaporator cool and low in pressure, and travels back down the suction line to the compressor.",
      "startMs": 134890,
      "durationMs": 5737
    },
    {
      "id": "cap-s5-2",
      "kind": "caption",
      "beatId": "s5-2",
      "label": "And that is the loop. Nothing was used u",
      "text": "And that is the loop. Nothing was used up. The same refrigerant will go around again in a few seconds, and keep going until the thermostat is satisfied.",
      "startMs": 141827,
      "durationMs": 8152
    },
    {
      "id": "cap-close-1",
      "kind": "caption",
      "beatId": "close-1",
      "label": "Compress, condense, meter, evaporate. Pr",
      "text": "Compress, condense, meter, evaporate. Pressure up, heat out, pressure down, heat in. Every reading you take and every part you replace sits somewhere on that circle.",
      "startMs": 151179,
      "durationMs": 9660
    }
  ],
